            <Text>Page {1_N} of {2_M}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_EXPANSION_INTRO_LAST_PAGE_HINT">
            <Text>Last page. Press Enter to continue to the game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_EXPANSION_INTRO_NAV_HINT">
            <Text>Press Right or N for next page, Left or P for previous, T to toggle "Do not show again", Control plus I for illustration description, Control plus T to re-read, Enter or Escape to close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_EXPANSION_INTRO_ILLUSTRATION_PLACEHOLDER">
            <Text>Illustration description not yet available.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_DONT_SHOW_AGAIN_ON">
            <Text>Do not show again, on.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_DONT_SHOW_AGAIN_OFF">
            <Text>Do not show again, off.</Text>
        </Row>

        <!-- Loading screen briefing (waypoint 04). Dawn of Man civ
             intro briefing + Ctrl+T/I/S hotkeys. -->
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_BRIEFING_HEADER">
            <Text>{1_Civ}. Join the world stage.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_ERA_FORMAT">
            <!-- Just the era name. Civ VI's era Name LOC already
                 includes the word "Era" ("Ancient Era", "Classical
                 Era", etc.) — appending " Era." here makes it
                 "Ancient Era Era." which is jarring. -->
            <Text>{1_Era}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_LEADER_INTRO">
            <!-- No trailing period — describer SHORT lines already
                 end with a period. Adding one made "world map.." -->
            <Text>{1_LeaderName}. {2_PortraitBrief}</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_FEATURES_HEADER">
            <Text>Unique abilities and features.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_HOTKEY_HINT">
            <Text>Press R to repeat the briefing. T re-reads abilities. I for leader description. S for Dawn of Man transcript.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_BRIEFING_DECISION_SEAN">
            <Text>Press Enter to start the Dawn of Man speech, or Escape to skip to the game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_POST_SEAN_PROMPT">
            <Text>Dawn of Man speech playing. Press Enter when you are ready to begin the game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_BRIEFING_DECISION_NOSEAN">
            <Text>Press Enter or Escape when ready to begin the game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_STARTING">
            <Text>Creating game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_STARTING_LOAD">
            <Text>Loading game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_STARTING_TUTORIAL">
            <Text>Loading tutorial.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_COMPLETE_READY">
            <Text>Loading complete. Press Enter or Escape to begin the game.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_PORTRAIT_PLACEHOLDER">
            <Text>Leader portrait description not yet available.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_LOAD_TRANSCRIPT_MISSING">
            <Text>Dawn of Man transcript not available for this leader.</Text>
        </Row>

        <!-- Scanner. SCANNER_HELP is the ? cheat-sheet (reword freely). The rest
             are the scanner's standalone spoken strings. (Category/subcategory
             labels still live in ScannerCore.lua and the per-instance announce
             format in ScannerNav.lua — pending the string-localization audit.) -->
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_SCANNER_HELP">
            <Text>Use the scanner to select terrain, cities, resoureces and other items on the map and then jump to the selected items. This may help facilitate unit placement or map exploration. Scanner keys are as follows: Press Page Down and Page Up to cycle between items, units, terrain etc. For example,  hills, forest, or a resource. Press alt plus Page Down or alt+Page Up to step through selected item types. For instance, if hills is selected, you would press alt+Page Up or alt+Page Down to cycle through the visible explored hills on the map.   Press control plus Page Down or control+Page Up to change to a main map category : for instance, units, terrain, resources, cities. Press Shift plus Page Up or shift+Page Down  to change to a map item subcategory. For instance, selecting city will allow you to pick tye type of city to list. Press home to jump thje map cursor  to the currently selected  item on the scanner. Press end to read its distance and direction.   Press backspace to return to your previous map location.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_SCANNER_EMPTY">
            <Text>Nothing here.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_SCANNER_HERE">
            <Text>Here</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_CIVVIACCESS_SCANNER_NO_RETURN">
            <Text>No jump to return from.</Text>
        </Row>

    </BaseGameText>
</GameData>
